      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Por la mañana, Hermod le rogó a Hel que dejara volver a Baldr. Todos lloraban por él, le dijo.",
          "en": "In the morning, Hermod begged Hel to let Baldr ride home. Everyone was weeping for him, he said."
        },
        {
          "es": "Hel respondió: «Entonces veremos si de verdad todos aman a Baldr».",
          "en": "Hel answered: “Then we will see if Baldr is truly loved by all.”"
        },
        {
          "es": "«Si todas las cosas del mundo lloran por él, vivas y muertas, volverá.»",
          "en": "“If everything in the world weeps for him, living and dead, he will go back.”"
        },
        {
          "es": "«Pero si una sola cosa se niega a llorar, se queda aquí, conmigo.»",
          "en": "“But if even one thing refuses to weep, he stays here, with me.”"
        },
        {
          "es": "Baldr acompañó a Hermod hasta la puerta. Le dio el anillo de oro Draupnir, para llevárselo a Odín.",
          "en": "Baldr walked Hermod to the door. He gave him the gold ring Draupnir, to take back to Odin."
        }
